# ===========================================================================
#  How git and GitHub should treat the files in this repository.
#
#  Taiyabah Masjid · Bolton Central Islamic Society · Charity 1041569
#  15 September 2026
#
#  WHY THIS EXISTS
#  ---------------
#  index.html is 624 KB of GENERATED output. Nobody writes it: build.py makes
#  it from index_template.html, and the rule everywhere else in this project
#  is "never edit index.html by hand". But git and GitHub did not know that,
#  so every push offered up an eight-thousand-line diff of machine output,
#  and every browser asked to render it sat there chewing.
#
#  That is what "git crashes on the HTML files" turned out to mean. It is not
#  a size problem — 624 KB is nothing — it is a RENDERING problem. A diff
#  viewer laying out a generated page full of inlined data, on a phone or a
#  modest laptop, stops responding. Nothing about the symptom says so.
#
#  `-diff` tells git to treat the file as binary FOR DIFF PURPOSES ONLY. It is
#  still a normal text file, still committed, still served. What changes is
#  that git and GitHub print "Binary files differ" instead of rendering eight
#  thousand lines nobody was ever going to read.
#
#  THE TRADE, SAID OUT LOUD: `git diff index.html` will no longer show you
#  what changed. That is the right way round HERE and would be wrong almost
#  anywhere else — the change you actually want to read is in
#  index_template.html, which is NOT listed below and diffs normally. If you
#  ever genuinely need the generated diff:
#
#      git diff --text index.html
#
#  `linguist-generated` is GitHub's own marker. It collapses the file in pull
#  requests and keeps it out of the language statistics, so the repository
#  stops describing itself as mostly HTML when the work is elsewhere.
# ===========================================================================

#  Generated by build.py. Read index_template.html instead.
index.html  linguist-generated=true -diff
404.html    linguist-generated=true -diff

#  Third-party, minified, one enormous line. Nobody reviews this either — it
#  is the Supabase client, dropped in as a file so the staff screens do not
#  depend on a CDN being up.
admin/supabase.js  linguist-vendored=true -diff

#  A year of prayer times, and the source of truth for them. It diffs fine
#  now that build.py writes one day per line, and a change to it is something
#  somebody SHOULD read — a transposed column here is the wrong Maghrib for a
#  whole month. Listed to say that the omission is deliberate.
#  build-inputs/full2026.json  — intentionally not marked.

#  Normalise line endings IN THE REPOSITORY only. A file opened and saved on
#  Windows comes back with every line marked as changed otherwise, which makes
#  a real one-line fix impossible to find in the diff.
#
#  Deliberately `text=auto` and NOT `eol=lf`. `eol=lf` would force LF into the
#  working copy as well, and a Windows editor that does not understand LF then
#  shows the whole file as a single line — which is precisely the kind of
#  "everything is broken" that this file exists to stop.
* text=auto

#  Except the things that are not text and must never be touched.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.pdf   binary
